# `$isAsBornExceptForAddedNames(object, maker)`: `$isAsBorn` WITH ONE CONDITION FEWER: values added under other names leave it true. The same stamped operation with one more engine flag: the emitter leaves the bit "has an extra property" out of the word that it asks.
# Behind the yes a read of a name of the literal is a read of a slot; a read under another name stays a lookup and finds what was added (ADDED: 1). The strict question is asked of the same object beside it.
# An accessor added under another name makes both false: such an object bears a mark, and the shape test refuses marked objects. False says nothing: what was added and deleted again leaves the strict form false (ADDEDANDDELETED), an accessor that was added and deleted again leaves both false.
